      "text": [
        " عَلِيٌّ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ : \"اَلْمُعْتَقُ عَنْ دُبُرٍ هُوَ مِنَ اَلثُّلُثِ وَ مَا جَنَى هُوَ وَ اَلْمُكَاتَبُ وَ أُمُّ اَلْوَلَدِ فَالْمَوْلَى ضَامِنٌ لِجِنَايَتِهِمْ \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3468 - Imam Ali ibn Abi Talib (as) said:\n\"A mudabbar (a slave promised freedom after the owner's death) is counted as part of the one-third (of the estate). As for any offense committed by the mudabbar, the mukatab (a slave under a contract of emancipation), or the umm al-walad (a bondwoman who bore her master a child), the master is liable for their offenses.\""
        ]
      }
    },
